# Git decides text-vs-binary by sniffing content, and it gets PDFs wrong: a
# PDF built from plain ASCII looks like text, so end-of-line conversion kicks
# in on checkout. That shifts every byte offset recorded in the file's xref
# table and the document stops opening. Mark the binary assets explicitly.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.jfif  binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
